            <ArticleTitle>Retrograde coronary sinus perfusion for management of coexistent critical unstable carotid and coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>717-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case report describes a difficult and not uncommon situation of a patient suffering from an evolving myocardial infarction with hemodynamic instability along with a critical bilateral extracranial carotid artery stenosis. A technique of retrograde coronary sinus perfusion was used to temporarily stabilize the cardiac status while the carotid lesion was being tackled.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
